---

🔓 Why Open Source?

Because a project becomes much more valuable when other people can learn from it.

You can:

- 👀 Read the source
- 🧠 Learn from the implementation
- 🛠️ Modify it
- 🐛 Report bugs
- 💡 Suggest features
- 🔀 Fork it
- 🤝 Contribute
- 🚀 Build something completely different from it

The code belongs to the community as much as possible.

---

🤝 Want to Help Without Donating?

You absolutely can.

⭐ Star a repository

A star helps people discover the project.

🐛 Report a bug

Found something broken?

Tell me.

💡 Suggest an idea

Your idea could become the next feature.

🔀 Contribute

Pull requests are welcome.

📢 Share

Sharing an open-source project can be just as valuable as financial support.

«Not everyone can donate money. Everyone can help in some way. ❤️»

---

❓ FAQ

<details>
<summary><b>💰 Why are you asking for funding?</b></summary><br>Open-source development can involve real costs such as hosting, domains, hardware, testing equipment and development infrastructure.

Funding helps keep projects running and gives me more resources to experiment and build.

</details><details>
<summary><b>🔓 Will the projects remain open source?</b></summary><br>The projects covered by open-source licenses will remain available under their respective licenses.

</details><details>
<summary><b>💵 Do I have to donate?</b></summary><br>No.

You can use the projects, star repositories, report bugs, suggest ideas or simply share them.

Every form of support is appreciated.

</details><details>
<summary><b>🏆 What happens if I donate?</b></summary><br>Depending on the contribution and whether you want recognition, supporters may be listed on the Supporter Wall.

Anonymous support is always welcome.

</details><details>
<summary><b>📊 Where does the money go?</b></summary><br>The current goal is intended for project-related expenses such as infrastructure, hosting, hardware, domains, security and development.

</details><details>
<summary><b>🧑‍💻 Can I contribute code?</b></summary><br>Yes.

Open an issue, fork a repository and submit a pull request.

</details>---

🌍 About Dörverden

<div align="center">🇩🇪 Dörverden • Lower Saxony • Germany

</div>I'm developing from Dörverden, a municipality in Lower Saxony near the Weser River.

It's a very different environment from the big technology hubs.

And that's part of the point.

«You don't need to live in Silicon Valley to build technology.»

You need curiosity, a computer, persistence and the willingness to keep learning.

